// «N» calls that each READ one cell of a module's state of «N» cells. Reading
// one cell does not depend on how many there are, so the whole is linear; an
// engine whose call costs the size of the state is quadratic.
<# ./mod/mesa => M
M::crear(«N»)
s = 0
@ k:1..«N» { s = s + M::leer((k % «N») + 1) }
>> s + M::cuanto() ¶
